-- 1804: Free-AI-subscription wording fixes, per the official MySkillsFuture rule (course must END on or
-- after 16 Sep 2026; the learner must COMPLETE it; SWDA emails the request form afterwards).
--  * post 206 (n8n, mig 1802): content rebuilt from the generator source -- 'complete', guide links.
--  * post 182 (launch explainer): 4 start-date sentences -> end-date, dead /contact-us link -> /contacts, update note linking the guide.
--  * category 313 (free-ai-subscription-courses) description: start-date sentence -> end-date.
--    Category FLAT tables are not touched here (they differ per partner); reindex catalog_category_flat after deploy.
-- Each REPLACE needle was probed on SG prod 2026-10-10 (exactly 1 match each). Re-runs are no-ops.
SET @is_sg := IF(@mms_instance = 'SG', 1, 0);
UPDATE mmd_blog_post SET content = '<p><strong>Short version:</strong> pick the one task that eats your week, such as sorting enquiry emails, copying form entries into a spreadsheet or chasing approvals, and spend three days building an n8n workflow with an AI agent that handles it for you. That is the outcome of <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-agentic-ai-automation-with-n8n.html">WSQ Agentic AI Automation with n8n</a>. Because the course carries the <em>Free AI sub</em> label on MySkillsFuture, eligible Singapore Citizens can also redeem six months of a premium AI tool after the course, which gives you time to keep improving the workflow on real work.</p> <h2>Start with the task, not the tool</h2> <p>Most people who try automation start with the software and look for something to point it at. It works better the other way round. Pick a task you can describe in one sentence, that happens at least weekly, and that follows roughly the same steps each time. An AI agent is useful where the steps need some judgement, for example reading a message and deciding what kind of request it is, not just moving data from A to B.</p> <table> <thead><tr><th>Task you do today</th><th>What the workflow does</th><th>Where the AI agent helps</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>Reading and routing enquiry emails</td><td>Watches the inbox, logs each enquiry, alerts the right person</td><td>Classifies the request and drafts a first reply</td></tr> <tr><td>Copying web-form entries into a sheet</td><td>Receives the form through a webhook and writes a clean row</td><td>Fixes messy free-text fields and flags incomplete entries</td></tr> <tr><td>Answering the same policy questions</td><td>Takes the question from chat or email and replies</td><td>Looks up your own documents (RAG) before answering</td></tr> <tr><td>Weekly status reporting</td><td>Pulls figures from your tools on a schedule</td><td>Summarises what changed and what needs attention</td></tr> <tr><td>Approvals that sit in someone''s inbox</td><td>Sends the request, waits, then continues</td><td>Prepares a summary so the approver can decide quickly</td></tr> </tbody> </table> <p>If a task needs a judgement call that you would not trust a new colleague with, keep a person in the loop. The course teaches that pattern on purpose.</p> <h2>What you build in three days</h2> <p>The course runs over three days (24 hours) and follows the order you would use to build a real workflow. Using the enquiry-email example, here is how the five topics map onto the build:</p> <ol> <li><strong>Workflow automation with n8n.</strong> Set up the trigger (a new email), the actions (log it, notify someone) and the connections to the apps you already use.</li> <li><strong>Agentic process automation with AI agents.</strong> Add an AI agent that reads each enquiry, decides what type it is and chooses the next step, instead of you writing a rule for every case.</li> <li><strong>Webhooks and HTTP requests.</strong> Connect systems that have no ready-made n8n node, such as an internal form, a booking system or a third-party API.</li> <li><strong>Agentic RAG.</strong> Let the agent look up your own price lists, FAQs or policies before drafting a reply, so answers are based on your information rather than the model''s guess.</li> <li><strong>Human-in-the-loop, monitoring and security.</strong> Route sensitive replies to a person for approval, catch and handle errors, and keep credentials and data safe before the workflow runs unattended.</li> </ol> <p>You leave with a working workflow and the know-how to build the next one yourself. n8n is a low-code tool, so you do not need to be a programmer. The entry requirements are a polytechnic diploma and at least one year of working experience, which also gives you real tasks to automate. See the full outline and upcoming dates on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-agentic-ai-automation-with-n8n.html">course page</a>.</p> <h2>The six months after class: where the free AI subscription comes in</h2> <p>A workflow is never finished on the last day of a course. You will find edge cases, refine prompts and add steps once real data starts flowing. That is what the SkillsFuture AI subscription is for. In SWDA''s words, it lets you &ldquo;apply what you have learnt to real use cases at work and in everyday life&rdquo;.</p> <p>Eligible learners choose one of five subscriptions. For someone building automations, this is how they compare:</p> <table> <thead><tr><th>Subscription</th><th>Useful for an automation builder when you&hellip;</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>ChatGPT Plus</td><td>want a strong all-round assistant to plan workflows, write and test prompts, and debug expressions or JSON</td></tr> <tr><td>Google AI Pro</td><td>work mainly in Gmail, Docs and Sheets and want Gemini built into those apps</td></tr> <tr><td>Microsoft 365 Personal</td><td>work mainly in Word, Excel, PowerPoint and Outlook and want Copilot built in</td></tr> <tr><td>Manus AI</td><td>want a general AI agent for research and multi-step knowledge work alongside your own workflows</td></tr> <tr><td>Singtel AI Pass</td><td>want to try a range of AI tools for three months before settling on one for the next three</td></tr> </tbody> </table> <p><strong>One thing to plan for:</strong> a consumer subscription is not the same as API access. The AI nodes inside n8n usually call a model through an API key, which providers normally bill separately on their developer platforms. Use the subscription as your thinking and debugging partner, and set aside a small budget for the API calls your workflow makes.</p> <h2>Who is eligible, and how redemption works</h2> <p>These rules come from SWDA''s official <a href="https://www.myskillsfuture.gov.sg/content/portal/en/career-resources/career-resources/education-career-personal-development/redeem-ai-subscription.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Redeem AI Subscription page</a>:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Who:</strong> Singapore Citizens aged 18 and above.</li> <li><strong>Which courses:</strong> you must enrol in and <strong>complete</strong> a course carrying the <em>Free AI subscription</em> label on MySkillsFuture, with a course end date <strong>on or after 16 September 2026</strong>. This course carries the label (TGS-2023035977).</li> <li><strong>How many:</strong> one subscription per person in total, however many eligible courses you attend.</li> <li><strong>When:</strong> access follows the course. It is not given when you enrol. After you complete the course, SWDA emails you the subscription request form and you have <strong>60 days from that email</strong> to choose your tool.</li> <li><strong>Your choice is final:</strong> you cannot change the subscription once the form is submitted. You receive the outcome and activation details by email.</li> </ul> <p>Singapore PRs and other learners can still take the course and use any course-fee funding they qualify for. They are not eligible for the subscription. For every step from the AI Ready Quiz to activation, see our <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/blog/how-to-claim-free-ai-subscription-singapore-eligibility-steps-courses">step-by-step claim guide</a>.</p> <h2>Course fee and funding</h2> <p>The subscription is separate from course-fee funding. You keep the usual WSQ subsidy, and the subscription is on top of it.</p> <table> <thead><tr><th>Learner</th><th>Funding</th><th>Nett fee (incl. GST)</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>Full fee</td><td>&ndash;</td><td>$1,308.00 ($1,200 + $108 GST)</td></tr> <tr><td>Singapore Citizen / PR aged 21+</td><td>50% WSQ funding</td><td>$708.00</td></tr> <tr><td>Singapore Citizen aged 40+ (MCES), or SME-sponsored</td><td>70% WSQ funding</td><td>$468.00</td></tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Singapore Citizens can use <strong>SkillsFuture Credit</strong> to offset the nett fee, and eligible companies can use SkillsFuture Enterprise Credit. Funding needs digital attendance via the Singpass app and a pass in the assessments. Check your exact amount when you <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-agentic-ai-automation-with-n8n.html">register on the course page</a>.</p> <h2>Where this fits in your learning pathway</h2> <p>Treat the n8n course as the point where AI moves from something you chat with to something that does work for you. A sensible route:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Before:</strong> if you have hardly used AI tools, spend a few weeks using a free AI assistant for everyday writing and research first. You will get much more from the agent topics.</li> <li><strong>After, if you lead a team or a business unit:</strong> <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-business-innovation-with-agentic-ai-and-ai-agents.html">Business Innovation with Agentic AI and AI Agents</a> moves from one workflow to deciding where agents should change how your organisation works.</li> <li><strong>After, if your work is marketing:</strong> <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/multi-ai-agents-workflow-for-content-creation.html">Multi AI Agents Workflow for Content Creation</a> applies the same multi-agent ideas to a content pipeline.</li> <li><strong>After, if you want to write code:</strong> <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-ai-vibe-coding-with-python.html">AI Vibe Coding with Python</a> covers the cases n8n nodes cannot handle.</li> </ul> <p>Take these follow-on courses for the skills. They do not earn another subscription, because the limit is one per person. If you are eligible, redeem it after whichever eligible course you take first, and choose the tool you will use on your workflows.</p> <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2> <div class="mmd-faq"> <details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I need to know how to code to learn n8n?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. n8n is a low-code, visual workflow tool. You connect nodes on a canvas. Some comfort with simple logic and with reading data such as JSON helps, and the course walks you through it.</p></div></details> <details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I get the free AI subscription as soon as I sign up?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. Redemption happens after you complete the course. You receive an email with the request form and have 60 days from that email to submit the request form. Activation details follow by email if your request is successful.</p></div></details> <details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Can I get a second subscription by taking another eligible course?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. Each eligible Singapore Citizen can redeem one subscription in total, regardless of how many eligible courses they attend.</p></div></details> <details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">I am a Singapore PR. Can I still take the course with funding?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Yes. Singapore PRs aged 21 and above qualify for 50% WSQ funding on this course. The free AI subscription is only for Singapore Citizens aged 18 and above.</p></div></details> <details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Will ChatGPT Plus pay for the AI calls my n8n workflow makes?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Usually not. Consumer subscriptions and API usage are normally billed separately, so plan a small API budget for workflows that run on their own. Use the subscription for designing, testing and debugging your workflows.</p></div></details> <details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Can I use SkillsFuture Credit for this course?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Yes. Eligible Singapore Citizens can use SkillsFuture Credit to offset the fee payable after WSQ funding.</p></div></details> </div> <h2>Next step</h2> <p>Write down the one task you would most like to stop doing by hand, then bring it to class. You will spend three days turning it into a working n8n workflow with an AI agent, with WSQ funding on the fee. If you are an eligible Singapore Citizen, you can then redeem a six-month AI subscription to keep refining it. <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-agentic-ai-automation-with-n8n.html">See dates and register for WSQ Agentic AI Automation with n8n</a>, or browse all <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/free-ai-subscription-courses.html">courses with a free AI subscription</a>. For eligibility and every claim step, read <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/blog/how-to-claim-free-ai-subscription-singapore-eligibility-steps-courses">how to claim your free AI subscription</a>.</p> <h3>Sources</h3> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.myskillsfuture.gov.sg/content/portal/en/career-resources/career-resources/education-career-personal-development/redeem-ai-subscription.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MySkillsFuture: Redeem AI Subscription to Further Your AI Learning</a> (SWDA, last updated 1 October 2026)</li> <li><a href="https://courses.myskillsfuture.gov.sg/courses/TGS-2023035977--Agentic-AI-Automation-n8n" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MySkillsFuture course listing: Agentic AI Automation with n8n (TGS-2023035977)</a></li> </ul>', updated_at = NOW() WHERE @is_sg = 1 AND url_key = 'automate-work-tasks-n8n-ai-agents-free-ai-subscription' AND content NOT LIKE '%how-to-claim-free-ai-subscription-singapore-eligibility-steps-courses%';
UPDATE mmd_blog_post SET content = REPLACE(content, 'who attend an eligible AI course starting <strong>1 September 2026 or later</strong> can claim', 'who complete an eligible AI course ending <strong>on or after 16 September 2026</strong> can claim') WHERE @is_sg = 1 AND url_key = 'free-ai-subscription-now-live-swda-eligible-courses' AND LOCATE('who attend an eligible AI course starting <strong>1 September 2026 or later</strong> can claim', content) > 0;
UPDATE mmd_blog_post SET content = REPLACE(content, 'with a start date of <strong>1 September 2026 or later</strong>.', 'with a course end date <strong>on or after 16 September 2026</strong>.') WHERE @is_sg = 1 AND url_key = 'free-ai-subscription-now-live-swda-eligible-courses' AND LOCATE('with a start date of <strong>1 September 2026 or later</strong>.', content) > 0;
UPDATE mmd_blog_post SET content = REPLACE(content, 'The <strong>course start date</strong> is what matters, not the enrolment date &mdash; a course that began in August does not qualify.', 'The <strong>course end date</strong> is what matters, not the enrolment date &mdash; a course that ended before 16 September 2026 does not qualify.') WHERE @is_sg = 1 AND url_key = 'free-ai-subscription-now-live-swda-eligible-courses' AND LOCATE('The <strong>course start date</strong> is what matters, not the enrolment date &mdash; a course that began in August does not qualify.', content) > 0;
UPDATE mmd_blog_post SET content = REPLACE(content, '<summary class="mmd-faq-q">My course started in August. Do I qualify?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Unfortunately not &mdash; the course must start on or after 1 September 2026. If you are close to that line, check your class start date before assuming either way.</p>', '<summary class="mmd-faq-q">My course ended before 16 September 2026. Do I qualify?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Unfortunately not &mdash; the course must end on or after 16 September 2026. If you are close to that line, check your class end date before assuming either way.</p>') WHERE @is_sg = 1 AND url_key = 'free-ai-subscription-now-live-swda-eligible-courses' AND LOCATE('<summary class="mmd-faq-q">My course started in August. Do I qualify?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Unfortunately not &mdash; the course must start on or after 1 September 2026. If you are close to that line, check your class start date before assuming either way.</p>', content) > 0;
UPDATE mmd_blog_post SET content = REPLACE(content, 'href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/contact-us"', 'href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/contacts"') WHERE @is_sg = 1 AND url_key = 'free-ai-subscription-now-live-swda-eligible-courses' AND LOCATE('href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/contact-us"', content) > 0;
UPDATE mmd_blog_post SET content = CONCAT('<p><em>Updated 10 October 2026:</em> SWDA&rsquo;s eligibility rule is based on the course <strong>end</strong> date, which must be on or after 16 September 2026. For every claim step, see our <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/blog/how-to-claim-free-ai-subscription-singapore-eligibility-steps-courses">guide to claiming the free AI subscription</a>.</p>', content), updated_at = NOW() WHERE @is_sg = 1 AND url_key = 'free-ai-subscription-now-live-swda-eligible-courses' AND content NOT LIKE '%how-to-claim-free-ai-subscription-singapore-eligibility-steps-courses%';
UPDATE catalog_category_entity_text t JOIN eav_attribute ea ON ea.attribute_id = t.attribute_id AND ea.attribute_code = 'description' AND ea.entity_type_id = 3 JOIN catalog_category_entity_varchar k ON k.entity_id = t.entity_id AND k.store_id = 0 AND k.value = 'free-ai-subscription-courses' JOIN eav_attribute ka ON ka.attribute_id = k.attribute_id AND ka.attribute_code = 'url_key' AND ka.entity_type_id = 3 SET t.value = REPLACE(t.value, 'Your class must start on or after 1 September 2026', 'Your course must end on or after 16 September 2026') WHERE @is_sg = 1 AND LOCATE('Your class must start on or after 1 September 2026', t.value) > 0;
